      "message": "I always find this logic difficult to get follow and there are still multiple instances of it in the file.\nOne thing you can do to simplify this is :\n- have a highestPermission(Boolean p1, Boolean p2)\n- use it here :\n  final Boolean permission \u003d highestPermission(getPackageNetdPermission(app), mApps.get(appId);\n- also use it in highestPermissionForUid :\n  final PackageInfo app \u003d mPackageManager.getPackageInfo(name, GET_PERMISSIONS | MATCH_ANY_USER);\n  return highestPermission(currentPermission, getPackageNetdNetworkPermission(app));\n\nAnother option is to stop using this bizarre Boolean scheme and switch to ints. Then you can just use \"\u003e\". I think that\u0027d be a lot more explicit.\n\nKeep in mind : I suspect there will be a day where permissions won\u0027t be strictly ordered, and instead will behave as a bitmask, so having something like highest() won\u0027t be an option. But that\u0027s not coming immediately.",
